WEBVTT

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:17.760
Mitsuhide-san!

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.620
Where am I?

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:28.600
Who am I?

00:02:04.830 --> 00:02:08.770
<i>It was a tiny whim that 
brought me in contact</i>

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:11.870
<i>with that terrible incident.</i>

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.220
Kibayashi-kun, stop here.

00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:21.050
Hey, who are you?

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:23.390
It looks like something happened here.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.490
I thought I'd take a look.

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.240
This place is off-limits.

00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:29.750
Get lost.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.250
Akechi-san!

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:33.010
That's you, isn't it, Akechi-san?

00:02:33.010 --> 00:02:34.070
Detective Hirai?

00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:37.500
Your assistant, Kibayashi, 
is with you, too, huh?

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:39.720
So you know the detective.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.010
This is the famous 
detective, Akechi-sensei.

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:48.000
So you're in charge of this 
crime scene, Detective Hirai?

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.440
I would be overjoyed to have 
the opinion of somebody

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:56.240
who's solved as many 
difficult cases as you.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.530
Come in.

00:03:05.490 --> 00:03:06.790
What on...

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:09.750
A single puncture wound to the 
heart, from the front.

00:03:10.160 --> 00:03:12.850
And she's so young, too. It's horrible.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:15.160
<i>A headless corpse?</i>

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:18.060
Who's the victim?

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:20.740
Her name is Hototogisu Ayako.

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.660
The eldest of the three 
Hototogisu sisters.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.720
They're a very old family in this area.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:28.270
Three sisters?

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:33.260
She has two younger sisters: 
Meiko and Machiko.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.300
They said that she was a 
very free-wheeling sort.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.820
That she had her quirks.

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:42.150
She would often leave the house

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.620
in the middle of the night and 
go swimming in this river.

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.290
Naked?

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:53.290
Indeed. We found her 
clothes a little upstream.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:57.690
<i>So that explains why she's naked.</i>

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:01.790
<i>The next question is why 
they cut her head off.</i>

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:11.350
Is something wrong?

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:13.620
There was a strange man over there.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.020
A strange man?

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:17.230
Kibayashi-kun, you saw him, too, right?

00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:20.810
Yes.

00:04:20.810 --> 00:04:24.240
I was passing by when I 
saw someone lying there.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:26.610
When I got closer...

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:28.240
It was Ayako-san?

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:29.530
Yes.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.120
I knew it was the eldest

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.750
daughter of the Hototogisu 
family at a glance.

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.000
Detective.

00:04:36.520 --> 00:04:37.960
The coroner confirmed our thoughts:

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.810
her heart was pierced.

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:41.880
Estimated time of death is

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.010
between 11:00 and midnight last night.

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:47.760
And there's no sign of any drug use.

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:49.850
Okay, I've got it!

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:51.100
Why?!

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.400
Why am I a suspect?!

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.210
Hazama-san, I've heard you didn't get

00:04:58.210 --> 00:05:01.070
along with Ayako-san when she was alive.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:04.110
Well, sure... we had our differences.

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.650
And you said repeatedly

00:05:05.650 --> 00:05:09.100
that some day you would kill her!

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:12.370
But that doesn't mean 
I really killed her!

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:14.970
You saw Ayako-san alone at night,

00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:17.970
and thought it was your 
chance, didn't you?

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.490
And so you tried to get even—

00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:24.580
Detective, she's innocent.

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.970
The victim was stabbed from the front.

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:31.300
There's no signs of a 
struggle, and no indication

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:33.470
that any drug was used 
to make her fall asleep.

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:37.580
And the victim was swimming 
naked in the river.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.570
Detective, would someone 
leave themselves so

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:43.730
exposed to a person who'd said repeatedly

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.100
they were going to kill them,

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.880
and let themselves be stabbed?

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:51.990
Well, you're right...

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:54.080
Okay, you're free to go!

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:59.420
But if it wasn't Hazama Okemi,

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:01.720
our next suspect is...

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.170
Sob sob.

00:06:06.460 --> 00:06:10.280
Our father, Genji, just died,

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:13.380
and now Ayako-neesan!

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.430
Sob sob!

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:19.360
I saw the body in the chapel after
it was returned from the coroners.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:21.730
At least it didn't look 
like she suffered much...

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:23.820
I guess that's some consolation.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.400
Sob sob!

00:06:26.130 --> 00:06:27.930
Indeed.

00:06:27.930 --> 00:06:28.750
But...

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.450
Henri!

00:06:31.030 --> 00:06:33.030
Yes, Miss Meiko.

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:39.310
But why are we suspects?

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:41.210
That's right.

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:44.260
Neither I nor Meiko-neesan 
have any alibi.

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.150
But that's because we 
were alone in our rooms.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:48.180
That's right.

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.500
It was the middle of the night, 
of course we were!

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:52.680
What are the police thinking?

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:54.520
Miss Meiko.

00:06:55.270 --> 00:06:56.930
Thanks, Henri!

00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:09.270
I never eat dinner without this.

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.960
I see.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:15.800
I'm told Akechi-san is a 
very famous detective.

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:17.430
I wouldn't go that far.

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.550
Please.

00:07:19.010 --> 00:07:22.920
Please prove our innocence 
and catch the real criminal!

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:29.270
You can stay here as long 
as you like until then.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:33.860
If you need something, tell Henri here.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:35.550
Thank you.

00:07:35.550 --> 00:07:37.010
I'm done.

00:07:37.010 --> 00:07:38.780
You're done already?

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:41.220
Yes. I'm full.

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:45.310
You barely ate a thing today...

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.000
That's right.

00:07:47.000 --> 00:07:49.320
You're on a diet, aren't you, Machiko?

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:51.180
I'm not on a diet!

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.600
I just don't feel like eating.

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:56.850
Such an awful thing just 
happened and look at you...

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:59.290
Sob sob!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:01.730
Henri, make sure you wrap up the rest

00:08:01.730 --> 00:08:03.180
and put it in the fridge.

00:08:03.180 --> 00:08:05.580
We shouldn't waste food.

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:07.920
Understood.

00:08:13.230 --> 00:08:14.090
<i>Ayako.</i>

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:15.340
<i>Meiko.</i>

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:16.600
<i>Machiko.</i>

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.260
<i>The three sisters of 
the Hototogisu family.</i>

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:23.310
<i>At the end of last month,</i>

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:25.790
<i>the head of the Hototogisu 
family, Genji, died of illness.</i>

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:31.240
<b>Hototogisu Genji                             Wife ?</b>

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:31.240
<b>Eldest - Ayako           2nd - Meiko           3rd - Machiko</b>

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:31.570
<i>And now his heir, Ayako, 
the eldest, was murdered.</i>

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:34.870
<i>From the state the body was found in,</i>

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:37.590
<i>it's very possible she was 
murdered by someone she knew.</i>

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:47.660
Did I imagine it?

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:58.620
This stuff's great on white rice!

00:08:58.620 --> 00:09:00.680
It stinks, Onee-sama.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:07.070
First, I have to investigate 
the crime scene more thoroughly.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:15.560
Him again?

00:09:16.160 --> 00:09:17.400
Thank you for coming.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.650
Did you find anything?

00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:25.320
No... that masked man's 
been staring at the scene.

00:09:27.270 --> 00:09:30.150
Oh, Professor Morilanty.

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.250
Morilan?

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:32.970
Morilanty.

00:09:32.970 --> 00:09:35.270
A strange man who lives on 
the edge of the village.

00:09:35.270 --> 00:09:38.340
He claims to be a professor 
of applied criminology,

00:09:38.340 --> 00:09:40.180
but who knows what he's really doing...

00:09:40.580 --> 00:09:42.190
Applied criminology?

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:45.880
He probably wants to 
investigate the case.

00:09:45.880 --> 00:09:48.110
You should stay away from him.

00:09:53.070 --> 00:09:56.590
This is the chapel where 
Ayako-san's body is being held.

00:09:57.320 --> 00:10:00.420
They must really be rich if they've

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.450
got a chapel on their property.

00:10:02.450 --> 00:10:05.280
Sensei, where have you been?

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:06.860
What's wrong, Kibayashi-kun?

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:08.210
Why are you in such a hurry?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.940
They found a new suspect!

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:13.460
Detective Hirai wants you 
to come to the station.

00:10:14.610 --> 00:10:17.220
His name is Murakumo Matsuo.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:21.050
He may dress like that, 
but he's definitely a man.

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:23.010
He's a well known blackmailer.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.260
The entire village hates him.

00:10:25.260 --> 00:10:30.770
His thug pals call him Matsuko 
the Spider, so I've heard.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:34.190
Come on, confess.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.250
Silence!

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:36.430
Don't tell me to be silent!

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:39.130
You killed Hototogisu Ayako!

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:43.240
What are you talking about? 
I don't have a clue!

00:10:43.540 --> 00:10:46.220
We've had our eye on him for a while.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.280
When we brought him 
in for something else,

00:10:48.280 --> 00:10:49.750
we found this.

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.020
What is it?

00:10:51.770 --> 00:10:53.750
The seal of the Hototogisu family.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.730
I'm told they have it specially made.

00:10:56.730 --> 00:10:58.070
Then...

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:00.760
We don't know what he was using to do it,

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:05.140
but we're confident Murakumo 
was blackmailing Ayako-san.

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:08.140
You were blackmailing Hototogisu Ayako.

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:10.170
But when you went to get the money,

00:11:10.170 --> 00:11:11.790
there was a problem and you killed her.

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:12.920
Right?

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:14.720
How stupid.

00:11:14.720 --> 00:11:17.060
I've been a blackmailer for years.

00:11:17.060 --> 00:11:18.900
I wouldn't screw up like that.

00:11:19.230 --> 00:11:21.200
Whether he's the criminal or not,

00:11:21.200 --> 00:11:23.330
I'm sure we can learn something from him.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.910
We'll pressure him until
he tells us something.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:42.080
I'm shocked.

00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:47.770
<b>Tenka 
Village 
Nude 
Murder 
Case</b>

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:47.770
So Murakumo was blackmailing 
Meiko-san, not Ayako-san!

00:11:47.770 --> 00:11:50.930
But how did you know, Akechi-san?

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:52.630
The smell.

00:11:52.630 --> 00:11:53.820
Smell?

00:11:53.820 --> 00:11:56.310
This stack of bills has a faint smell

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:57.940
of fermented soybeans.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.760
The ones that Meiko-san was 
always putting on her food.

00:12:02.810 --> 00:12:04.480
I see.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.090
So the smell of the soybeans 
stuck to her fingers

00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:09.450
and transferred to the 
bills without her knowing.

00:12:09.770 --> 00:12:13.580
But now the investigation is 
back to square one, Sensei.

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:15.350
Indeed...

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:17.150
The time when Meiko-san went

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:19.080
to meet Murakumo for the trade overlaps

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:21.120
almost completely with Ayako-san's

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:22.650
estimated time of death.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:25.440
There's a long distance 
between the place they met

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:26.820
and the crime scene.

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.720
The time involved makes it impossible 
for her to have done it.

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:31.750
Your Rairaiken ramen is here!

00:12:31.750 --> 00:12:35.960
But why didn't Meiko-san 
say anything about it?

00:12:35.960 --> 00:12:39.850
If only she had, we would've 
stopped suspecting her.

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:42.440
Three bowls of ramen, 1800 yen.

00:12:42.860 --> 00:12:45.280
Given what she was 
being blackmailed for.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.780
Thank you.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:48.420
She must've been too
worried about being exposed

00:12:46.780 --> 00:12:50.200
Here's 8200 yen in change.

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:50.200
to say anything.

00:12:51.310 --> 00:12:52.650
Goodnight!

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:56.210
Even if that meant being 
suspected of her sister's murder?

00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:02.670
Actually, I'm not related 
to my father, Genji.

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:08.140
I'm the illegitimate child of 
my mother and another man.

00:13:08.140 --> 00:13:09.680
If it gets out,

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:14.650
I won't be able to inherit 
the Hototogisu family.

00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.690
Sob sob!

00:13:18.990 --> 00:13:22.540
Murakumo was blackmailing her

00:13:22.540 --> 00:13:26.630
with an old diary Genji's wife kept.

00:13:26.630 --> 00:13:29.840
It talks about her lover and

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:35.660
the child she's carrying... likely Meiko.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:42.040
It says very clearly that the 
child isn't her husband's.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:47.300
So that clears Hazama 
Okemi, Murakumo Matsuo,

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:49.060
and Hototogisu Meiko.

00:13:49.060 --> 00:13:50.730
That leaves...

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:52.680
Machiko, the youngest.

00:13:53.030 --> 00:13:57.560
There's also the possibility 
it was a random murder.

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:59.380
No, Detective.

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:01.410
That would be disappointing.

00:14:02.300 --> 00:14:04.690
Disappointing? To whom?

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.610
To me.

00:14:07.730 --> 00:14:09.700
I see.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:12.970
Give me a moment.

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:16.740
My little goma tofu-colored cells are

00:14:16.740 --> 00:14:19.190
working at full capacity.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.320
I'm counting on you.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.550
I know.

00:14:26.550 --> 00:14:28.530
What if Machiko-san was the one

00:14:28.530 --> 00:14:31.850
who put Murakumo up to blackmailing her?

00:14:32.200 --> 00:14:33.390
What if?

00:14:33.940 --> 00:14:35.980
Her goal would've been

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:39.770
to take away Meiko-san's 
alibi during the murder.

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.760
While Murakumo was 
meeting with Meiko-san,

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:47.530
she went and killed Ayako-san.

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:52.050
And so, Meiko-san has a firm alibi,

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:56.320
but can't say anything about it.

00:14:56.320 --> 00:14:57.500
Indeed.

00:14:57.780 --> 00:15:02.530
If we hadn't brought in 
Murakumo for something else,

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:05.980
Meiko-san would still 
be our prime suspect.

00:15:07.260 --> 00:15:09.430
Okay, I've got it!

00:15:09.820 --> 00:15:13.670
Let's take another look at Machiko-san.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:18.660
There's no need for that, Detective.

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:19.770
Henri-san?

00:15:20.170 --> 00:15:24.270
Miss Machiko has a firm alibi.

00:15:24.270 --> 00:15:25.270
What?

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:30.920
Miss Machiko has been on a 
diet for the past month.

00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:34.560
She always leaves more 
than half her meals.

00:15:34.560 --> 00:15:39.770
But dinner that night was 
her favorite, fish tempura.

00:15:40.260 --> 00:15:42.830
Even so, she managed to avoid eating

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:45.540
almost anything during dinner,

00:15:45.540 --> 00:15:49.170
but when I went to the 
kitchen that night...

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:53.030
Miss Machiko!

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:54.670
What's wrong?

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:56.900
My stomach...

00:15:57.650 --> 00:16:00.100
just started hurting.

00:16:00.570 --> 00:16:03.630
She ate something full of fat

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:06.290
while being on such a limited diet.

00:16:06.290 --> 00:16:09.110
It left her with a bad stomachache.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.090
She had some medicine and

00:16:11.090 --> 00:16:13.160
got better shortly afterwards,

00:16:13.160 --> 00:16:15.230
but not to the point where

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:18.570
she could have left the 
mansion to kill someone.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.010
Why didn't you tell us that sooner?

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:26.360
Miss Machiko insisted I didn't.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:28.480
It would embarrass the 
family if it was known

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:30.370
that a daughter of the Hototogisu

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:33.100
collapsed after eating a midnight snack.

00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:37.840
But still, it hurt to conceal 
the truth from the police,

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:42.390
so I've come to tell you the truth.

00:16:42.390 --> 00:16:45.050
Henri-san, I hate to say this,

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:47.130
but it's possible, since you're her servant,

00:16:47.130 --> 00:16:49.150
you're making this up to protect her.

00:16:49.540 --> 00:16:53.680
No, this is the complete truth.

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:57.700
I am prepared to state 
so formally if required.

00:16:59.250 --> 00:17:01.700
<i>Meiko and Machiko didn't do it.</i>

00:17:03.990 --> 00:17:07.110
<i>Then who did?</i>

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:11.450
<i>And why did they cut off the head?</i>

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:14.130
<i>Why would they...</i>

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.390
<i>A headless body.</i>

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:19.850
<i>A mask.</i>

00:17:20.450 --> 00:17:21.920
They switched places?

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:36.530
There he is!

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.530
Wait!

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:44.670
Wait!

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:01.050
Morilanty!

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:05.520
You're going to show 
me who you really are!

00:18:09.600 --> 00:18:11.070
Give it up!

00:18:14.260 --> 00:18:15.630
Kibayashi-kun?

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:17.620
No...

00:18:17.620 --> 00:18:21.400
Morilanty is actually you?

00:18:22.280 --> 00:18:25.490
No. Professor Morilanty's true identity

00:18:25.490 --> 00:18:27.550
is not young Kibayashi.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:31.250
Kibayashi's true identity 
is Professor Morilanty.

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:32.850
That's the same thing!

00:18:32.850 --> 00:18:35.260
It's not, Sensei.

00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:39.930
Kibayashi-kun?

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:43.530
What's... What's going on here?

00:18:44.810 --> 00:18:46.310
This.

00:18:51.890 --> 00:18:54.650
I've been with you this whole time.

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:57.320
I've always been watching you.

00:18:57.850 --> 00:18:59.740
But why?

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:04.420
Because you... are the criminal!

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:06.250
W-What are you saying?

00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:08.300
I'm the detective!

00:19:08.300 --> 00:19:09.880
I can't be the criminal!

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:11.530
Then tell me this.

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:13.950
Why are you the only one who

00:19:13.950 --> 00:19:17.920
thinks it's a headless corpse, 
when it still has a head?

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:23.140
Because you don't want to 
accept whose body it is.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.000
What?

00:19:25.000 --> 00:19:28.450
That was clearly a headless body!

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:30.170
Then how did the person

00:19:30.170 --> 00:19:31.520
who found it so quickly

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:33.610
realize it was Hototogisu Ayako,

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:36.650
when the body was naked?

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:41.790
Because he saw her face.

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:43.590
Why else?

00:19:43.590 --> 00:19:47.100
And do you remember what Machiko-san said

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:48.370
when they were eating?

00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:50.950
I saw the body in the chapel

00:19:50.950 --> 00:19:53.070
after it was returned from the coroners.

00:19:53.070 --> 00:19:55.950
At least it didn't look 
like she suffered much...

00:19:57.030 --> 00:19:59.170
It didn't look like she suffered

00:19:59.170 --> 00:20:01.630
because her face looked peaceful.

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:02.880
Am I wrong?

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:08.390
You killed someone very dear to you.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:12.140
But you didn't want to admit it.

00:20:13.330 --> 00:20:15.190
No...

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:18.340
That's impossible!

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:22.510
Come on, you still have your last line.

00:21:24.060 --> 00:21:25.470
Say it.

00:21:26.360 --> 00:21:30.510
That one sentence will end this play.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:32.630
I...

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:35.020
Yes, you...

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:42.480
I...

00:21:58.790 --> 00:22:02.070
I am Akechi Mitsuhide?

00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:05.550
I...

00:22:06.210 --> 00:22:07.510
I...

00:22:08.980 --> 00:22:10.580
I killed Nobunaga-sama!

00:23:46.040 --> 00:23:46.980
Lick.

00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:49.280
These are the Vengeful Fangs!

00:23:49.280 --> 00:23:50.870
Akechi Mitsuhide!

00:23:50.870 --> 00:23:53.270
Next time on Sengoku Collection:

00:23:53.270 --> 00:23:55.780
"Vengeful Fang - OS."

00:23:55.780 --> 00:23:57.410
Watch the next episode, too, okay?

00:23:57.410 --> 00:23:58.430
Yay!
